summary:
The long-lived waste (lifetime 2000 t, reach kept at 22 px) was re-run on three more seeds with their own mutation draws: seed 10 with its twin to T=10000, and seeds 13 and 14 to T=8000. Mean distance of a vortex's trait from the ancestor per 2000 t:
- seed 7 (20261028T0105): 0.24, 0.89, 1.19, 1.84, 2.43;
- seed 10: 0.25, 0.77, 1.39, 1.36, 1.15;
- seed 13: 0.33, 0.84, 1.16, 1.33;
- seed 14: 0.29, 0.67, 0.92, 1.20;
- twins: 0.14-0.49.
With the standard waste over the same t=6000-8000 window, seeds 3-6 give 0.96-1.2.
Share on new ground (more than 0.4 from every trait seen before t-1000), by 1000-t window:
- seed 10: 0.21, 0.25, 0.07, 0.07, 0.15, 0.03, 0.09, 0.00;
- seed 13: 0.24, 0.35, 0.04, 0.06, 0.04, 0.00;
- seed 14: 0.03, 0.07, 0.02, 0.17, 0.04, 0.00.
Cloud radius at the end: 0.93-1.05.
On seed 10 a purple kind swept and then a second lineage invaded from t~5800 and coexisted (m10_spec_maps.png), so the population branched instead of travelling. The memory-only arm (lifetime 2000 t, reach 45 px, seed 7) is intermediate: mean distance 1.47, cloud radius rising to 0.82, new-ground share 0.03-0.54. c58-style counts still exceed the twin on every seed: classes held by >= 3 vortices 44/43/40 (twin 20 on seed 10), and 3-16 first-time dominants after t=3000. A labkit pack of the long-memory world (seeds 11 and 12, T=3000) reproduces c53's fed-vortex individuals and reticulate division: about 34 vortices, 48 and 55 persistent splits, generation 13 and 12, merge/split 0.92 and 0.93.
